# PR Quality Bar

A PR is an argument to a reviewer{{REVIEWER_CONTEXT}}, not a diff dump.
<!-- REVIEWER_CONTEXT: " (CodeRabbit + a human)" / " (future-you; solo repo)" etc. from interview. -->

- **Every PR answers "what problem does this solve?"** in its first sentence. "Add feature X" is a title, not a problem.
- **One ticket per PR.** Unrelated improvements you found become new tickets, not stowaways.
- **Small enough to review in one sitting.** If the ticket forces a big diff, structure the description to guide the reading order.
- **Description = problem, approach, verification.** Approach says why this way; verification says what you ran and what a reviewer can click/run to confirm.
- **The diff matches the description.** Before opening, re-read the diff and remove or explain anything a reviewer would ask "why is this here?" about.
- Use `/create-pr`; it enforces all of the above.
